WEBVTT

00:01:31.670 --> 00:01:34.190
We passed the initial screening 
of the Idol Festival!

00:01:34.190 --> 00:01:37.950
Green Leaves Entertainment

00:01:35.920 --> 00:01:39.810
These are the groups participating 
in the Tohoku preliminaries.

00:01:37.970 --> 00:01:40.990
<b>Idol Festival</b>

00:01:39.810 --> 00:01:40.990
It's finally starting.

00:01:41.340 --> 00:01:43.310
Only the group that scores highest

00:01:43.310 --> 00:01:46.280
based on on-line and off-line fan votes

00:01:46.280 --> 00:01:54.090
and the judge's scores 
will make it to the I-1 Arena.

00:01:54.710 --> 00:01:57.970
Everyone's so cute.

00:01:57.970 --> 00:01:59.470
Hey, look at this.

00:02:00.220 --> 00:02:01.470
Are they entertainers?

00:02:01.470 --> 00:02:03.810
They're so unique.

00:02:03.810 --> 00:02:07.470
They've got an incredible 
aura in more than one way...

00:02:07.470 --> 00:02:11.370
But don't they seem more 
like comedians than idols?

00:02:11.370 --> 00:02:14.520
You're right. I don't 
think we'll lose to them.

00:02:14.520 --> 00:02:16.860
Don't be stupid.

00:02:17.250 --> 00:02:20.690
You'll run into trouble 
if you underestimate them.

00:02:20.690 --> 00:02:21.460
What?

00:02:21.460 --> 00:02:23.280
You don't understand, do you?

00:02:23.280 --> 00:02:26.090
These comedic groups 
are the real danger.

00:02:26.090 --> 00:02:27.050
What?

00:02:27.770 --> 00:02:31.650
Plenty of idol groups are 
good at singing and dancing.

00:02:31.650 --> 00:02:33.270
The groups that make

00:02:33.270 --> 00:02:36.760
the strongest impact 
in the judges' eyes control the game.

00:02:36.760 --> 00:02:41.910
In that respect, the Demons of Oga 
are doing better than us.

00:02:41.910 --> 00:02:44.210
Yes, but...

00:02:44.210 --> 00:02:46.640
What is the essence of Wake Up, Girls!?

00:02:47.290 --> 00:02:49.140
Think about it.

00:02:51.150 --> 00:02:53.650
<b>Kumagaiya</b>

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:53.650
What is WUG's essence, huh?

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:55.810
I wonder what it is.

00:02:55.810 --> 00:02:57.150
It's a difficult question.

00:02:57.960 --> 00:03:00.250
We've been working so hard overcoming

00:03:00.250 --> 00:03:02.040
the challenges we've encountered.

00:03:02.040 --> 00:03:04.050
I don't know what makes us unique.

00:03:04.050 --> 00:03:08.660
I've never seen such excited fans before.

00:03:08.980 --> 00:03:12.180
They've certainly captured 
the interest of their fans.

00:03:12.180 --> 00:03:14.290
The president's right.

00:03:14.630 --> 00:03:18.000
The preliminaries will be streamed lived

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:21.250
and fans will vote in real time, right?

00:03:21.250 --> 00:03:23.800
We can't win if we don't 
make an impression.

00:03:24.340 --> 00:03:26.820
We still have time. 
Let's come up with something.

00:03:26.820 --> 00:03:29.410
But I haven't thought about it before.

00:03:29.410 --> 00:03:31.310
Do you have any questions?

00:03:31.310 --> 00:03:31.690
Yes!

00:03:32.050 --> 00:03:37.050
What do you think is 
the appeal of Wake Up, Girls!?

00:03:38.550 --> 00:03:39.940
<b>Local Gourmet Super Delicious</b>

00:03:38.550 --> 00:03:39.940
<b>Event Details</b>

00:03:39.060 --> 00:03:39.940
What?

00:03:41.760 --> 00:03:44.250
The appeal of Wake Up, Girls!?

00:03:44.250 --> 00:03:44.950
Yes.

00:03:44.950 --> 00:03:46.080
<b>Serious Idol Talk! 

00:03:46.620 --> 00:03:50.560
This is our 50th concert at MACANA.

00:03:50.560 --> 00:03:54.610
Oh, right. There's something 
we want to ask you today.

00:03:54.610 --> 00:03:55.810
Ask us anything!

00:03:55.810 --> 00:03:56.840
We'll answer your question!

00:03:58.340 --> 00:04:01.230
Anyway, when I asked...

00:04:01.230 --> 00:04:04.090
Maybe it's the way you eat, Minami-chan.

00:04:04.090 --> 00:04:07.180
That's only your appeal.

00:04:08.370 --> 00:04:09.960
Oh, I know.

00:04:09.960 --> 00:04:15.150
We've heard positive things about 
your biting comments, Kaya-chan.

00:04:15.350 --> 00:04:17.860
That only applies to you.

00:04:18.230 --> 00:04:19.480
Your naiveté!

00:04:20.510 --> 00:04:22.150
Your energy!

00:04:22.990 --> 00:04:24.460
Your shakiness!

00:04:27.280 --> 00:04:29.970
We got a lot of nonsense answers after that,

00:04:29.970 --> 00:04:34.010
such as how we're like dogs or plastic bags.

00:04:34.010 --> 00:04:36.140
We didn't get any helpful answers.

00:04:36.140 --> 00:04:39.880
Anyway, let's focus on our lessons.

00:04:39.880 --> 00:04:42.060
I doubled our training time and content.

00:04:42.060 --> 00:04:44.300
What? We're doing even more?

00:04:44.730 --> 00:04:48.330
Mayushi, can you watch us dance 
before the instructor gets here?

00:04:48.330 --> 00:04:49.010
Okay.

00:04:49.010 --> 00:04:51.760
It'd be great if you could take 
note of anything that sticks out.

00:04:51.760 --> 00:04:52.830
Got it.

00:04:54.110 --> 00:04:57.560
I'm glad everything worked out.

00:04:58.310 --> 00:04:59.680
Nanamin?

00:04:59.680 --> 00:05:03.380
Airi, try dancing the steps 
for the second Melody A section.

00:05:03.380 --> 00:05:04.030
What?

00:05:04.030 --> 00:05:05.300
I told you.

00:05:05.300 --> 00:05:09.090
My goal is to place first 
in the Idol Festival.

00:05:09.090 --> 00:05:12.040
I always meet my goals.

00:05:12.570 --> 00:05:15.790
In order to do that, 
I need you to work harder.

00:05:15.790 --> 00:05:17.790
What?!

00:05:38.560 --> 00:05:40.060
<b>Thank You for the Full House</b>

00:05:38.560 --> 00:05:40.060
<b>Adult</b>

00:05:45.600 --> 00:05:47.330
It's finally the weekend.

00:05:47.330 --> 00:05:48.130
Yeah.

00:05:48.130 --> 00:05:51.350
I hope we make it through 
this stage to the finals.

00:05:51.350 --> 00:05:53.330
Yeah. I want to win, too.

00:05:53.690 --> 00:05:55.540
You just wait, Tokyo!

00:05:55.540 --> 00:05:56.080
Yeah!

00:05:57.570 --> 00:06:00.340
Hey, you gals.

00:06:04.400 --> 00:06:07.590
Y'all are Wake Up, Girls!, right?

00:06:08.590 --> 00:06:12.270
Um, I don't understand 
what you're saying...

00:06:12.270 --> 00:06:13.130
Yeah, we are.

00:06:13.130 --> 00:06:13.950
What?

00:06:13.950 --> 00:06:17.100
Are you from Demons of Oga?

00:06:17.800 --> 00:06:20.850
Oh, so you know about us?

00:06:20.850 --> 00:06:23.320
'Course she does. We're famous.

00:06:23.320 --> 00:06:24.360
'Course.

00:06:24.760 --> 00:06:27.290
Guess we don't need 
to introduce ourselves, then.

00:06:27.290 --> 00:06:28.900
Do you need something?

00:06:28.900 --> 00:06:32.060
We thought we'd check out the girls

00:06:32.060 --> 00:06:34.620
we're gonna beat in the preliminaries.

00:06:34.990 --> 00:06:36.470
I see.

00:06:37.080 --> 00:06:42.730
We eat cute little idol groups 
like you for breakfast.

00:06:42.730 --> 00:06:44.250
Prepare yourselves!

00:06:44.250 --> 00:06:46.150
You're the ones who need 
to watch out for us.

00:06:46.150 --> 00:06:48.130
Y-Yoppi...

00:06:48.130 --> 00:06:51.100
Really? You've got some guts there.

00:06:51.100 --> 00:06:53.890
Are you the head of Wake Up, Girls!?

00:06:53.890 --> 00:06:55.890
Not the head. The leader.

00:06:56.440 --> 00:06:58.010
They're the same thing.

00:06:58.010 --> 00:07:02.190
I'm head of the Demons of Oga, 
Kinumiya Saki.

00:07:02.190 --> 00:07:07.240
These are our members:
Rokudai Yoko and Kazayama Yui.

00:07:07.670 --> 00:07:11.660
We look forward to meeting you again!

00:07:16.410 --> 00:07:19.260
I know we'll cream you 
in the preliminaries.

00:07:20.980 --> 00:07:23.400
What was that? A threat?

00:07:23.400 --> 00:07:24.450
How terrifying.

00:07:24.450 --> 00:07:25.840
What? It was?

00:07:25.840 --> 00:07:28.670
The president was right. They're strong.

00:07:29.400 --> 00:07:30.170
I'm home.

00:07:36.400 --> 00:07:39.010
Why are you starting this again?

00:07:39.010 --> 00:07:40.280
I...

00:07:40.280 --> 00:07:43.550
How much more do you 
have to make me suffer?

00:07:53.990 --> 00:07:54.450
Um...

00:07:56.450 --> 00:07:58.200
Wait, Mom!

00:07:58.200 --> 00:08:00.340
I'm sorry I haven't 
talked to you about

00:08:00.340 --> 00:08:04.090
what I'm doing with Wake Up, Girls!

00:08:04.090 --> 00:08:06.220
I don't care about that anymore.

00:08:07.400 --> 00:08:09.590
Please! I want you to listen.

00:08:23.390 --> 00:08:26.920
I want to tell you how I feel today.

00:08:28.180 --> 00:08:30.860
I know apologizing for hurting you

00:08:31.680 --> 00:08:35.360
over I-1 isn't enough,

00:08:35.990 --> 00:08:36.890
but...

00:08:38.030 --> 00:08:40.620
I couldn't stay there.

00:08:42.480 --> 00:08:48.310
It's hard to explain, 
but I wasn't happy there.

00:08:48.870 --> 00:08:55.130
I'm just sorry I hurt 
you and Dad because

00:08:56.000 --> 00:08:58.140
of my selfishness.

00:08:58.740 --> 00:09:04.000
My new agency is small, 
but the president, the manager,

00:09:04.000 --> 00:09:07.080
and all the members are doing their best.

00:09:07.680 --> 00:09:10.440
Everyone's so considerate of everyone else.

00:09:10.440 --> 00:09:13.370
Because of that, we fight sometimes,

00:09:13.370 --> 00:09:18.160
but I finally think this is where I belong.

00:09:18.530 --> 00:09:23.350
You may not understand, 
but I feel like I could be happy there.

00:09:24.680 --> 00:09:25.900
So, Mom...

00:09:27.670 --> 00:09:31.430
I told you before, but why 
don't you do whatever you want?

00:09:31.430 --> 00:09:34.170
Mom, this weekend, the Idol Festival

00:09:34.690 --> 00:09:37.300
regional preliminaries are happening.

00:09:37.800 --> 00:09:39.680
I'd like you to come watch.

00:09:39.680 --> 00:09:44.010
If you see me on stage, 
I think you'll understand.

00:09:52.820 --> 00:09:54.570
<b>Idol Festival</b>

00:09:56.570 --> 00:10:02.830
<b>Idol Festival 2014</b>

00:09:57.590 --> 00:10:02.830
<i>The Idol Festival symbolizes 
this age of warring idols.</i>

00:10:03.480 --> 00:10:06.310
<i>This event, planned 
and produced by head</i>

00:10:06.310 --> 00:10:11.590
<i>of the I-1 Club, 
Shiraki Tooru, has begun.</i>

00:10:11.960 --> 00:10:16.120
<i>The favorite of the highly contested 
Tohoku Block is Crescent Moon.</i>

00:10:16.120 --> 00:10:19.140
<i>Gathering sudden attention 
with the addition of former</i>

00:10:19.140 --> 00:10:20.670
<i>I-1 member, Shimada Mayu,</i>

00:10:20.670 --> 00:10:24.830
<i>the one-year-old Wake Up, Girls! 
is also a formidable contender.</i>

00:10:25.730 --> 00:10:29.290
<i>At first, only former I-1 member 
Mayu received attention,</i>

00:10:29.290 --> 00:10:32.700
<i>but through local 
broadcasts and concerts,</i>

00:10:32.700 --> 00:10:35.360
<i>the hard work of the other members 
has captured the attention of fans,</i>

00:10:35.360 --> 00:10:38.750
<i>and they have distinguished themselves.</i>

00:10:39.360 --> 00:10:41.370
Hey!

00:10:41.370 --> 00:10:44.370
Hey! Sorry we're late!

00:10:45.000 --> 00:10:46.960
The war council will now begin!

00:10:46.960 --> 00:10:47.750
Yeah!

00:10:48.060 --> 00:10:53.330
Today's subject: How can we show 
WUG fans are in the audience

00:10:53.330 --> 00:10:57.260
and support the girls 
on the day of the event?

00:10:57.760 --> 00:10:59.560
I've already thought of something!

00:10:59.560 --> 00:11:02.010
Why don't we make matching sweatshirts?

00:11:03.140 --> 00:11:07.340
These will not only unite our hearts,

00:11:07.340 --> 00:11:13.640
but also declare our presence 
to idol fans across the nation!

00:11:13.640 --> 00:11:15.340
They'll be black, right?

00:11:15.340 --> 00:11:18.610
And they'll say, "You can do it! 
Wake Up, Girls!", right?

00:11:16.530 --> 00:11:20.030
<b>You can do it!</b>

00:11:20.030 --> 00:11:22.910
All right! Let's keep our spirits high!

00:11:20.030 --> 00:11:23.910
<b>Family Cafe Diner</b>

00:11:22.910 --> 00:11:23.910
Yeah!

00:11:23.910 --> 00:11:25.910
Please keep your voices down.

00:11:25.910 --> 00:11:28.370
Oh, excuse us...

00:11:32.850 --> 00:11:34.540
Hello.

00:11:35.030 --> 00:11:36.500
Oh, it's been a while.

00:11:36.850 --> 00:11:38.260
It's good to see you again.

00:11:38.260 --> 00:11:39.950
So flashy.

00:11:39.950 --> 00:11:41.810
Hayasaka-san wants us to wear these?

00:11:41.810 --> 00:11:43.280
But they're so cute.

00:11:43.280 --> 00:11:44.760
We can win with these alone.

00:11:45.110 --> 00:11:47.340
Everyone seems so excited.

00:11:47.340 --> 00:11:48.420
I suppose.

00:11:48.420 --> 00:11:52.200
It would've been better if we'd had 
this solidarity earlier, though.

00:11:52.870 --> 00:11:55.770
But if we make it through 
the Tohoku preliminaries,

00:11:55.770 --> 00:12:00.180
maybe I'll treat those 
girls to something.

00:12:00.180 --> 00:12:01.940
You're going to jinx them.

00:12:01.940 --> 00:12:03.200
How rude.

00:12:03.570 --> 00:12:06.780
Hayasaka-san wrote you 
a new song, didn't he?

00:12:06.780 --> 00:12:11.750
Yes. It's so hard, he must 
have done it to spite us.

00:12:11.750 --> 00:12:13.570
You should be glad it's worth learning.

00:12:13.570 --> 00:12:15.320
Well, yes.

00:12:15.320 --> 00:12:18.420
Oh, right. Could we 
ask you something?

00:12:19.380 --> 00:12:20.170
Pork buns?

00:12:20.550 --> 00:12:22.550
No, bean buns.

00:12:22.550 --> 00:12:25.330
I found them in the convenience 
store the other day.

00:12:26.070 --> 00:12:28.430
The essence of Wake Up, Girls!, huh?

00:12:28.780 --> 00:12:29.340
Yes.

00:12:29.340 --> 00:12:33.940
Maybe you don't need to decide 
for yourselves what that is.

00:12:33.940 --> 00:12:34.690
What?

00:12:34.690 --> 00:12:36.180
You're right.

00:12:36.180 --> 00:12:40.700
I think the people who see 
you perform will decide for you.

00:12:42.190 --> 00:12:43.970
<b>Office for Rent</b>

00:12:45.500 --> 00:12:47.440
Well, we'd better get going.

00:12:47.440 --> 00:12:49.840
Make sure you win those preliminaries.

00:12:49.840 --> 00:12:50.700
Okay!

00:12:52.210 --> 00:12:53.100
Excuse me.

00:12:56.760 --> 00:13:00.510
I think I finally understand 
what you told us before.

00:13:01.830 --> 00:13:02.970
About fighting.

00:13:03.640 --> 00:13:06.040
Are you guys fighting enough?

00:13:06.450 --> 00:13:08.470
You should tell each other 
what you want to say.

00:13:08.990 --> 00:13:10.810
You're part of the same group.

00:13:11.880 --> 00:13:14.230
It took me long enough, though.

00:13:14.540 --> 00:13:15.520
I see.

00:13:15.520 --> 00:13:16.390
That's great.

00:13:17.010 --> 00:13:17.900
Yes.

00:13:19.740 --> 00:13:22.320
Leader, everyone's calling you.

00:13:22.320 --> 00:13:24.730
Oh, sorry. I'll be right there.

00:13:24.730 --> 00:13:26.200
Hey, Leader!

00:13:26.720 --> 00:13:27.660
You can do it.

00:13:34.790 --> 00:13:37.290
<b>Idol Festival</b>

00:13:36.390 --> 00:13:40.290
Mayu-chan, you need to leave soon.

00:13:43.680 --> 00:13:46.260
I hope you do well.

00:13:46.260 --> 00:13:49.670
I'll make your favorite tonight.

00:13:49.670 --> 00:13:50.300
Okay.

00:13:51.020 --> 00:13:52.250
See you later.

00:13:56.020 --> 00:13:57.620
<b>Tohoku Block Preliminaries</b>

00:14:00.240 --> 00:14:01.270
Good morning!

00:14:01.270 --> 00:14:02.130
<b>You can do it!</b>

00:14:02.150 --> 00:14:03.650
Hey!

00:14:06.650 --> 00:14:08.410
We should show our support, too!

00:14:09.270 --> 00:14:11.400
Let's start with a Minami chant!

00:14:11.400 --> 00:14:12.450
Yeah!

00:14:12.450 --> 00:14:13.630
Ready, and...

00:14:13.630 --> 00:14:17.320
Everyone's little sister, Minami!

00:14:17.320 --> 00:14:19.880
Minami-chan's so popular.

00:14:19.880 --> 00:14:21.170
She certainly is.

00:14:21.560 --> 00:14:23.590
We should do our best, too.

00:14:23.590 --> 00:14:26.920
I made these for today.

00:14:28.620 --> 00:14:31.180
Why are you so nervous?

00:14:32.200 --> 00:14:33.700
What about you, President?

00:14:33.700 --> 00:14:36.180
Also, you can't smoke here.

00:14:37.110 --> 00:14:38.110
Okay, okay.

00:14:38.110 --> 00:14:40.340
I can do it. I can do it if I try.

00:14:40.340 --> 00:14:41.600
I'm a shining star.

00:14:41.600 --> 00:14:42.570
What are you talking about?

00:14:42.570 --> 00:14:44.090
We're just entering the ready room.

00:14:44.090 --> 00:14:46.190
The battle has already begun.

00:14:46.190 --> 00:14:47.690
You're right.

00:14:49.380 --> 00:14:50.430
Yoppi?

00:14:52.060 --> 00:14:54.450
Come to get crushed by us?

00:14:54.450 --> 00:14:56.850
What? Say that again.

00:14:56.850 --> 00:14:58.420
Don't fight.

00:14:58.420 --> 00:15:00.330
Let's settle this on the stage.

00:15:00.330 --> 00:15:02.310
Bring it on.

00:15:03.590 --> 00:15:05.840
Was that...

00:15:06.310 --> 00:15:09.090
Yeah, the Demons of Oga.

00:15:09.480 --> 00:15:14.470
Thank you for coming 
to the Idol Festival today.

00:15:14.470 --> 00:15:16.910
The idol group that wins will be

00:15:16.910 --> 00:15:20.850
officially recognized 
as the I-1 Club's rival.

00:15:20.850 --> 00:15:24.230
<b>You can do it, Minami-chan!</b>

00:15:21.380 --> 00:15:27.610
This group will become the second 
most popular idol group in Japan.

00:15:27.940 --> 00:15:30.010
Hello, everyone.

00:15:30.010 --> 00:15:33.370
I'm general manager of the I-1 Club, 
Shiraki Tooru.

00:15:34.200 --> 00:15:38.600
The day of the Tohoku Regional 
Preliminaries has finally arrived.

00:15:38.600 --> 00:15:42.870
Aomori, Iwate, Akita, Miyagi, 
Yamagata, and Fukushima.

00:15:43.330 --> 00:15:48.630
Today, the top ten teams chosen 
via document screening and

00:15:48.630 --> 00:15:52.860
on-line polls will compete 
in the I-1 Sendai theater.

00:15:53.640 --> 00:15:58.890
Ten idol groups born from this 
region will battle here today.

00:15:59.370 --> 00:16:02.250
Only one group will make it to the finals,

00:16:02.250 --> 00:16:07.800
but let's show support for every 
idol group appearing here today.

00:16:08.580 --> 00:16:10.920
I'd now like to announce the opening of the

00:16:10.920 --> 00:16:13.910
Idol Festival Tohoku 
Regional Preliminaries.

00:16:16.160 --> 00:16:17.500
Saki-chan!

00:16:17.500 --> 00:16:18.410
Yoko!

00:16:18.750 --> 00:16:19.460
Yui-Yui!

00:16:19.460 --> 00:16:20.660
Demons!

00:16:24.300 --> 00:16:25.420
Let's go, girls.

00:16:25.420 --> 00:16:26.710
Yeah.

00:16:37.250 --> 00:16:39.680
Next up is Wake Up, Girls!!

00:16:39.680 --> 00:16:40.550
Let's go!

00:16:40.550 --> 00:16:41.680
Let's do it!

00:16:41.680 --> 00:16:43.440
Wake Up, Girls!!

00:16:45.890 --> 00:16:48.320
We are Wake Up, Girls!!

00:16:48.320 --> 00:16:50.120
Thank you for your support!

00:16:50.940 --> 00:16:53.190
WUG-chan!

00:16:59.300 --> 00:17:02.450
This is "First-Rate Smile!"

00:17:06.710 --> 00:17:09.960
<i>A schedule written in the clouds</i>

00:17:09.960 --> 00:17:13.420
<i>Filling an empty weekend</i>

00:17:13.420 --> 00:17:19.350
<i>With anything you can isn't right</i>

00:17:18.470 --> 00:17:19.970
<i>It's not right</i>

00:17:20.280 --> 00:17:23.520
<i>Only truly plain and ordinary days</i>

00:17:23.520 --> 00:17:26.900
<i>I film videos of my cat</i>

00:17:26.900 --> 00:17:32.190
<i>Maybe I'll try redecorating 
my room sometime</i>

00:17:32.190 --> 00:17:38.950
<i>I made a slideshow of my friends</i>

00:17:38.950 --> 00:17:43.500
<i>Full of smiles, full-on smiles everywhere</i>

00:17:43.500 --> 00:17:45.660
<i>Smiles, so many smiles</i>

00:17:45.660 --> 00:17:52.590
<i>I end up smiling, I have energy now</i>

00:17:52.590 --> 00:18:00.260
<i>I'll never give up, not in 
spring, summer, fall, or winter</i>

00:18:00.260 --> 00:18:03.770
<i>Because we've known painful seasons</i>

00:18:03.770 --> 00:18:07.020
<i>I appreciate unchanging smiles</i>

00:18:07.020 --> 00:18:10.480
<i>The smiles of Japan overwrite</i>

00:18:10.480 --> 00:18:13.780
<i>Even during hard times</i>

00:18:13.780 --> 00:18:17.200
<i>The smiles of Japan 
make things cuter</i>

00:18:17.200 --> 00:18:20.530
<i>The overflowing color 
of cherry blossoms</i>

00:18:20.530 --> 00:18:23.740
<i>Because we've known painful seasons</i>

00:18:23.740 --> 00:18:25.410
<i>First-rate smile</i>

00:18:25.410 --> 00:18:27.400
<i>Smile</i>

00:18:35.910 --> 00:18:37.530
Thank you very much!

00:18:37.530 --> 00:18:39.630
Thank you!

00:18:55.520 --> 00:18:56.560
It's over.

00:18:56.560 --> 00:18:59.030
Now we just have to 
wait for the results.

00:18:59.790 --> 00:19:03.210
We will now announce the results.

00:19:07.040 --> 00:19:09.540
<i>Wake Up, Girls!, please!</i>

00:19:10.460 --> 00:19:13.790
We will now announce 
the results of the Tohoku Block.

00:19:13.790 --> 00:19:14.830
This is it.

00:19:16.380 --> 00:19:20.410
The idol group with the highest score based

00:19:20.410 --> 00:19:27.790
on the off-line and on-line votes and 
the judge's scores will advance to the finals.

00:19:21.220 --> 00:19:29.680
<b>Results</b>

00:19:30.400 --> 00:19:34.190
The winner of the Tohoku Block is...

00:19:37.430 --> 00:19:39.510
Wake Up, Girls!!

00:19:42.460 --> 00:19:43.590
Did we win?

00:19:44.220 --> 00:19:45.330
No way...

00:19:45.330 --> 00:19:46.960
All right!

00:19:46.960 --> 00:19:48.790
We did it!

00:19:48.790 --> 00:19:50.290
All right!

00:19:51.220 --> 00:19:53.360
Amazing!

00:19:52.420 --> 00:19:54.570
I'm so happy!

00:19:54.570 --> 00:19:57.120
We're advancing to the finals!

00:19:57.120 --> 00:20:00.550
We did it! We really did it!

00:20:00.550 --> 00:20:02.680
Yeah, we did it.

00:20:05.430 --> 00:20:08.590
All right!

00:20:10.230 --> 00:20:15.350
We will now hand the Tohoku 
Block trophy to Wake Up, Girls!.

00:20:20.960 --> 00:20:21.710
Hey.

00:20:21.710 --> 00:20:22.860
What?

00:20:24.310 --> 00:20:27.900
Your performance was amazing.

00:20:27.900 --> 00:20:30.870
Go win the finals for us.

00:20:31.710 --> 00:20:33.610
We will. Thanks.

00:20:34.380 --> 00:20:38.290
We visited all the Tohoku idol groups,

00:20:38.290 --> 00:20:41.200
but yours had the most backbone.

00:20:41.610 --> 00:20:42.580
I see.

00:20:43.940 --> 00:20:47.520
Starting tomorrow, we're going 
back to working every day.

00:20:47.520 --> 00:20:49.890
We haven't given up.

00:20:51.480 --> 00:20:52.640
You can do it.

00:20:52.640 --> 00:20:56.260
If you lose the finals, 
we'll make you regret it.

00:20:56.260 --> 00:20:57.390
Thanks.

00:20:58.440 --> 00:21:00.400
You were great.

00:21:00.710 --> 00:21:02.030
What?

00:21:08.160 --> 00:21:10.660
Green Leaves Entertainment

00:21:09.390 --> 00:21:10.660
Good morning.

00:21:12.100 --> 00:21:14.600
Um, what did you want to talk about?

00:21:15.860 --> 00:21:17.920
It's your contract with us.

00:21:17.920 --> 00:21:21.160
You didn't join through the audition,

00:21:21.160 --> 00:21:24.060
so you hadn't formally signed on with us.

00:21:25.170 --> 00:21:26.930
<b>Shimada Mari</b>

00:21:25.940 --> 00:21:26.930
This is...

00:21:26.930 --> 00:21:30.450
Your mother came to the agency yesterday.

00:21:30.450 --> 00:21:34.360
She asked us to look after her daughter.

00:21:38.080 --> 00:21:39.190
It's great news.

00:21:39.910 --> 00:21:40.820
Yes.

00:21:42.070 --> 00:21:43.690
Good morning.

00:21:43.690 --> 00:21:46.800
I-1 should be appearing 
on a talk show today.

00:21:46.800 --> 00:21:50.200
I wonder if they'll mention 
the Idol Festival.

00:21:50.200 --> 00:21:55.460
<b>I-1 Club performs its new song!!</b>

00:21:50.870 --> 00:21:53.020
This is our new song 
that goes on sale today.

00:21:53.020 --> 00:21:55.460
It's by Hayasaka-san.

00:21:55.920 --> 00:21:57.750
It's a very difficult song.

00:21:57.750 --> 00:22:00.430
The choreography is incredibly challenging.

00:22:00.430 --> 00:22:02.460
But that's what makes it worth doing.

00:22:02.900 --> 00:22:05.720
This is "First-Rate Smile"!

00:22:06.040 --> 00:22:08.220
What? This song title...

00:22:08.570 --> 00:22:10.220
Isn't that our song?

00:22:11.030 --> 00:22:11.970
It can't be!

00:22:11.970 --> 00:22:14.970
To be continued

00:23:44.980 --> 00:23:47.500
<b>Next Episode Preview</b>

00:23:45.380 --> 00:23:47.160
Ai-chan, what are you good at?

00:23:47.160 --> 00:23:48.850
Making sweets, I guess.

00:23:48.850 --> 00:23:51.160
That doesn't help you 
with your idol work.

00:23:51.160 --> 00:23:53.830
What? But sweets would be 
a great present for fans.

00:23:53.830 --> 00:23:56.200
I'm not into that kind of flattery.

00:23:56.200 --> 00:23:57.350
What?

00:23:57.350 --> 00:23:59.620
The next episode is 
"Idol Rhapsody!"

00:23:57.350 --> 00:23:59.660
<b>"Idol Rhapsody"</b>

00:23:59.640 --> 00:24:01.640
<b></b>
